the clark county school bus drivers are  getting a raise now the move comes after  a shortage of bus drivers during the  pandemic mary jane belliesa shares how  ccsd employees are hoping this will help  solve the problem  latrice mcallen has been a driver with  ccsd for four years she says it's a  passion to work with kids and says the  pay increase is a good way to recognize  the hard work bus drivers have to put in  every day it's going to benefit me in a  lot of ways the pay increase i'm a  single parent  gas is high  rent is going up so i'm very pleased  with the pay raise executive director of  transportation jennifer vovis says the  pay increase comes after an evaluation  with the district ccsd deemed  transportation employees to a higher pay  grade after reviewing job duties  responsibilities and performance  everybody's been very excited about it  i've heard a lot of anecdotal stories  i myself had a driver who  was put in their two weeks notice and  after the announcement was made they  rescinded their two weeks notice i've  heard drivers say that they now they can  quit their second job starting pays at  21.50 for bus drivers that's a six  dollar increase from before the district  hopes that all pay increases for all  positions will help with retention and  future hires currently there are 250 bus  driver vacancies daniel mack hayward has  been a driving instructor for 17 years  she's seen her fair share of people come  and go it's an incentive for the  instructors because now we can be more  competitive with other jobs so as people  come in they'll be willing to stay and  further their  opportunities in the district reporting  from weltman way and las vegas boulevard  mary jane balleza live local now
 

